We consider the following class of gradient systems in one unbounded spatial
  dimension:

  \begin{equation}
  \label{eq:1}
  u_t = \Delta u + f(u)
  \end{equation}

  where $f$ is a smooth function satisfying the following conditions:

  \begin{enumerate}
  \item $f(0) = 0$
  \item $f(u) > 0$ for $u > 0$
  \item $f(u) < 0$ for $u < 0$
  \item $f'(u) > 0$ for $u > 0$
  \item $f'(u) < 0$ for $u < 0$
  \end{enumerate}

  We prove that the global behaviour of bistable solutions is determined by
  the asymptotic behaviour of the solution at infinity.

